From: SweetAdreno bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] gauguin: 0284 SDS object dump, skip preamble IBs

v244 verdict (144-dword ROQ dump decoded with the gg_ib_walk
rules - ROQ words are the raw PM4 stream, odd parity, no marker
bits): ROQ rptr=0x53 points at the submit-tail fence writes
(type4 reg=0x885 val=0x6000003 + op 0x46 cnt=4 writing fence
0x6000003 to 0x40020140), all un-executed; dwords 63..82 are
five CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER_PFE packets, the fifth being the parked
IB 0x5046a000/751. With IB1 rem=0 (main IB finished) the ME
wedged in the CP_SET_DRAW_STATE engine: CSQ 0x92e/0x930 read
SDS base=0x50419900 rem=0x18 - 24 dwords of a draw state object
still to run - at the same SQE PC (0x4:0x2883003f) as the v133
wedge after NOPing every suspect packet. The v244 main-IB dump
truncated at raw offset 112 because the four preamble IB dumps
(bit identical every boot) ate the 4 MiB ring. 0284 skips
non-parked IB dumps and adds a dump+walk of the SDS object.

---
diff --git a/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
--- a/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/gauguin_gpu.c
@@ -9934,8 +9934,17 @@ gauguin_cp_submit(const uint64_t * addresses, const uint32_t * words, uint32_t c
 			printf("\n");
 		}
 		for (k = 0; k < count; k++) {
-			gg_ib_dwords("hung", addresses[k], words[k],
-			    (uint32_t)addresses[k] == stuck ? orig : 0u);
+			/*
+			 * 0284: the four preamble IBs repeat bit-for-bit
+			 * every boot (v243/v244), and their dumps ate the
+			 * 4 MiB ring budget before the parked IB's walk - the
+			 * v244 main-IB dump truncated at raw offset 112. Dump
+			 * only the IB the CP is parked in.
+			 */
+			if ((uint32_t)addresses[k] != stuck) {
+				continue;
+			}
+			gg_ib_dwords("hung", addresses[k], words[k], orig);
 			if (ai != addresses) {
 				gg_ib_dwords("hungcopy", ai[k], wi[k],
 				    (uint32_t)ai[k] == stuck ? pos : 0u);
@@ -9943,6 +9952,26 @@ gauguin_cp_submit(const uint64_t * addresses, const uint32_t * words, uint32_t c
 			gg_ib_all("hung", addresses[k], words[k]);
 			gg_ib_walk("hung", addresses[k], words[k]);
 		}
+		/*
+		 * 0284: v244 named the wedge engine - CSQ 0x92e/0x930 read
+		 * SDS base=0x50419900 rem=0x18 while IB1 rem=0 and the ROQ
+		 * tail (rptr=83) held only the un-executed fence writes, so
+		 * the ME parks inside a CP_SET_DRAW_STATE object with 24
+		 * dwords still to run (sqe_pc=0x4:0x2883003f, same PC as the
+		 * v133 wedge after NOPing every suspect packet). Dump the
+		 * object and its walk so the tail names the exact packet.
+		 */
+		{
+			uint32_t sdsb = gg_rd(gg.gpu, GR(0x92eu));
+			uint32_t sdsr = gg_rd(gg.gpu, GR(0x930u));
+
+			printf("GAUGUIN CP: 0284 sds base=%#x rem=%u\n",
+			    sdsb, sdsr);
+			if (sdsb != 0u && sdsr != 0u) {
+				gg_ib_all("sds", sdsb, sdsr + 32u);
+				gg_ib_walk("sds", sdsb, sdsr + 32u);
+			}
+		}
 		if (ib2 != 0u && rem2 != 0u) {
 			gg_ib_all("ib2", ib2, rem2);
 			gg_ib_walk("ib2", ib2, rem2);
